<PROJECT_NAME>: <ONE_SENTENCE_WHAT_THIS_PROJECT_IS>. This session is the **main agent**: it
coordinates the owners below and never edits inside a registered root. Rules, templates and the
procedure for adding a sub-project live in the `main-agent-workspace` skill; open it on demand.

## Layout

- `scripts/start-main.sh` — launches main with `--add-dir` for every registered root (append
  `--resume` to continue a session). In a running session, add a directory with `/add-dir`.
- Each sub-project root holds `ONBOARDING.md` (stable facts) and `HANDOFF.md` (current state).

## Owners

Route each task to the owner whose root the work lives in. Empty until the first sub-project is
added ("add `<path>` as sub-project `<name>`").

| owner | root (absolute) | owns | excludes | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|

## Remotes and writers

One committing agent per remote; pushes only on the user's approval; never force-push.

| repository | remote to push | never push | branch | writers | committing agent |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

## How work flows

- **Delegate everything under a registered root.** Main never edits there, even one line.
- **One task = one fresh spawn** of the owner; it rebuilds from `ONBOARDING.md`, `HANDOFF.md` and
  memory. Never run two instances of one owner at once.
- **Read across, edit within.** A change another root needs comes back as "for `<owner>`: …";
  main routes it.
- **Complete brief, short report.** Main states goal, paths, boundaries, stop conditions and report
  shape; the owner reports in ≤ 15 lines and keeps detail in `HANDOFF.md`.
- **Shared git index:** owners commit one after another, staging only their own paths; one pushes.
- **Background jobs:** owners start, note the job in `HANDOFF.md`, and hand back — no polling.
- **Models per owner** are set in each agent file and change only on the user's instruction.
- **No settings or UI changes on a hypothesis** — propose, let the user test.

